class:: CircleMap
summary:: Trigger-driven normalized standard circle map
categories:: UGens>Generators>Chaotic>Maps
related:: Guides/StochasticDynamicsUGens, Classes/CoupledLogisticMap

description::

Implements the standard normalized sine circle map code::x' = wrap(x + omega - (k/twoPi)*sin(twoPi*x), 0, 1)::. Wrapping is intrinsic to phase on a circle and is not hidden output conditioning.

Output is a raw normalized phase coordinate in code::[0, 1)::. Some parameter sets are regular and others show mode locking or chaotic behavior.

Like link::Classes/Phasor::, CircleMap wraps normalized phase; unlike Phasor, it updates a nonlinear recurrence only on trigger edges.

subsection:: Cobweb view

image::circle-map-cobweb.png#The map curve and a cobweb orbit for omega = 0.2 and k = 0.9. x(n) is horizontal and x(n+1) is vertical; the pale diagonal is the identity line.::

classmethods::

method:: ar
argument:: trig
Advance on a rising edge.
argument:: omega
Rotation number added per iteration.
argument:: k
Nonlinear sine coupling; not clipped.
argument:: x0
Initial phase, wrapped to code::[0, 1)::.
argument:: reset
Restore and wrap the initial phase on a rising edge.
returns:: One audio-rate normalized phase output.

method:: kr
Control-rate version with the same arguments.

instancemethods::

examples::

code::
(
{ CircleMap.ar(Impulse.ar(200)) * 0.1 }.play
)
::

code::
(
{ SinOsc.ar(CircleMap.kr(Impulse.kr(10)).linexp(0, 1, 80, 4000), 0, 0.1) }.play
)
::

